":"6b176876-1558-470a-abee-197b39057fc3","timestamp":"2026-11-27T18:49:21.392Z","tool_use_result":{"content":"{\"requestId\":\"94c6110c-e90f-4f16-88ad-5382f93d7e6b\",\"data\":[{\"id\":\"facebook_1088847760284220\",\"collationId\":\"1395452092789787\",\"platform\":\"facebook\",\"status\":\"inactive\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-09-13T05:51:59.406Z\",\"firstSeenAt\":\"2026-09-12T07:00:00.000Z\",\"lastSeenAt\":\"2026-10-05T08:31:30.991Z\",\"daysRunning\":23,\"media\":{\"type\":\"image\",\"thumbnailUrl\":null,\"mediaUrl\":\"https://medias.trendtrack.io/facebook/image/a33f135ac8bbad196a57ef191a8100ce376dabace75a4c3ac9f9bccac628493e.png\"},\"advertiser\":{\"id\":\"101838912282067\",\"name\":\"Lisa Anderson\",\"logoUrl\":\"https://medias.trendtrack.io/profile_picture/101838912282067.jpg\",\"facebookPageId\":\"101838912282067\",\"liveAdsCount\":139,\"reach30d\":324,\"totalReach\":1188914,\"countriesCount\":3,\"facebookLikes\":299,\"instagramFollowers\":null},\"content\":{\"title\":null,\"body\":\"My husband died a week ago.\\n\\nAnd there’s one photo on my phone I still can’t bring myself to delete.\\n\\nHe’s asleep in his recliner after dinner.\\n\\nMouth open.\\n\\nTV still on.\\n\\nGlasses and coffee sitting beside him.\\n\\nI took it because I thought it was funny.\\n\\nNow I look at that photo and wonder how many times his body was trying to tell us something we dismissed as “just getting older.”\\n\\nBecause that was our explanation for everything.\\n\\nThe naps after dinner.\\n\\nFalling asleep halfway through a movie.\\n\\nSaying he felt worn out even when he hadn’t done much that day.\\n\\nHe was 61.\\n\\nOf course he was more tired than he used to be.\\n\\nAt least that’s what we told ourselves.\\n\\nThen his cholesterol numbers started worrying his doctor.\\n\\nThat didn’t scare us much either.\\n\\nHe didn’t look sick.\\n\\nHe still cut the grass.\\n\\nStill drove our granddaughter to school when our daughter worked early.\\n\\nStill argued with our son about football every Sunday.\\n\\nStill complained whenever I bought the “healthy” bread.\\n\\nSo we did what we thought responsible people were supposed to do.\\n\\nWe changed breakfast.\\n\\nEggs became oatmeal.\\n\\nButter disappeared.\\n\\nI started checking labels at the grocery store.\\n\\nHe walked more.\\n\\nWe ordered fish instead of burgers.\\n\\nHe even stopped buying the cookies he’d eaten with his coffee for probably 20 years.\\n\\nEvery few months, there was another little sacrifice.\\n\\nAnd every time, he’d joke:\\n\\n“At this rate, you’ll have me eating cardboard by Christmas.”\\n\\nWe laughed.\\n\\nBut I could tell it bothered him.\\n\\nBecause food slowly stopped being something he enjoyed.\\n\\nIt became something he negotiated with.\\n\\nCan I eat this?\\n\\nHow bad is that?\\n\\nShould I skip dessert?\\n\\nMaybe I shouldn’t have the potatoes.\\n\\nAnd underneath all of it was the same belief:\\n\\nIf his cholesterol was high, he must still be eating the wrong foods.\\n\\nSo whenever his numbers weren’t where he wanted them, we blamed dinner.\\n\\nThen breakfast.\\n\\nThen snacks.\\n\\nThen ourselves.\\n\\nThat’s the part I keep thinking about now.\\n\\nBecause after he died, I sat at our kitchen table with his paperwork spread everywhere.\\n\\nOld blood work.\\n\\nAppointment notes.\\n\\nMedication lists.\\n\\nReceipts he’d stuffed into the same folder for reasons I’ll never understand.\\n\\nI wasn’t looking for anything specific.\\n\\nI think I just wanted to understand him.\\n\\nAnd somewhere between those pages, I realized how simplistic our thinking had become.\\n\\nWe had reduced cholesterol to a plate of food.\\n\\nEat the “bad” thing → cholesterol goes up.\\n\\nEat the “good” thing → cholesterol goes down.\\n\\nBut cholesterol is more complicated than any single breakfast or dinner.\\n\\nYour body produces cholesterol too, and factors beyond one meal can influence your overall numbers.\\n\\nThat sounds obvious when I write it now.\\n\\nIt didn’t feel obvious when we were standing in the grocery aisle debating whether he was “allowed” to buy cheese.\\n\\nThat realization sent me down a rabbit hole.\\n\\nNot because I thought I could go backward.\\n\\nI can’t.\\n\\nAnd I’m not going to pretend a supplement could have changed what happened to my husband.\\n\\nBut I needed to understand why we'd spent so much time treating every plate like it was the whole problem.\\n\\nEventually my reading led me to Ceylon cinnamon.\\n\\nI'd heard about cinnamon before.\\n\\nWhat caught my attention wasn't simply the ingredient.\\n\\nIt was how it was being delivered.\\n\\nCinnamon contains naturally occurring compounds including cinnamaldehyde.\\n\\nAnd cinnamaldehyde is fat-soluble.\\n\\nThat made me look differently at the dry cinnamon capsules I'd seen for years.\\n\\nPowder.\\n\\nCapsule.\\n\\nSwallow.\\n\\nDone.\\n\\nThen I found Primal Remedies.\\n\\nThey pair true Ceylon cinnamon from Sri Lanka with MCT oil inside an oil-based softgel.\\n\\nThe MCT oil acts as a lipid carrier for the fat-soluble cinnamon compounds.\\n\\nThey call the approach the Fat-Soluble Absorption Pathway.\\n\\nThat was what finally made the formulation make sense to me.\\n\\nNot “take more cinnamon.”\\n\\nThink about how the cinnamon is delivered.\\n\\nI also learned there is a meaningful difference between Ceylon cinnamon and the common cassia cinnamon most people recognize.\\n\\nCeylon naturally contains much lower levels of coumarin.\\n\\nAnd after everything I'd just been reading about health, I wasn't interested in blindly taking spoonfuls of random cinnamon from the kitchen cabinet.\\n\\nI wanted something simple that could fit beside the habits I was already trying to improve.\\n\\nSo I started using Primal Remedies Ceylon Cinnamon + MCT Oil as nutritional support alongside those habits.\\n\\nNot instead of eating well.\\n\\nNot instead of moving.\\n\\nAnd certainly not instead of speaking with a doctor and getting cholesterol checked.\\n\\nBecause if losing my husband taught me anything, it's that guessing how healthy someone is because they “look fine” isn't enough.\\n\\nLast Sunday, our daughter came over with the grandchildren.\\n\\nMy grandson climbed into Grandpa's recliner.\\n\\nSame chair from that photo.\\n\\nWithin 20 minutes, he was asleep sideways with one sock missing while everyone else was talking.\\n\\nFor half a second, I almost reached for my phone.\\n\\nThat's what I always did when his grandfather fell asleep like that.\\n\\nThen I stopped.\\n\\nThat chair doesn't make me laugh the same way anymore.\\n\\nBut it reminds me why I'm paying attention now.\\n\\nI don't want every meal to become a punishment.\\n\\nI don't want to spend the rest of my life afraid of breakfast.\\n\\nI just want to understand what I'm putting into my body, support it intelligently, keep getting my numbers checked, and be here for as many noisy Sunday afternoons with my family as I can.\\n\\nIf cholesterol has turned every plate in your house into a calculation, start by talking with your healthcare professional and understanding your actual numbers.\\n\\nAnd if you're already making healthier changes and want to learn about the Ceylon cinnamon + MCT oil approach I've added to my own routine, you can read about Primal Remedies below.\\n\\nBecause sometimes the photograph you thought was ordinary becomes the one that changes how you look at everything.\",\"transcript\":null,\"callToAction\":\"LEARN MORE\",\"landingPageUrl\":\"https://primal-remedies.com/pages/adv1-news-cinnamon\",\"landingPageDomain\":\"primal-remedies.com\",\"ctaDescription\":\"The Photo I Can't Look at the Same Way Anymore\",\"ctaLinkDescription\":\"🚨 UPDATE: Ceylon Cinnamon 7200mg is SELLING OUT faster than expected! Lock in your order NOW to get 70% OFF + FREE Shipping\"},\"metrics\":{\"reach\":132059,\"aggregatedReach\":null,\"estimatedSpend\":1189,\"duplicates\":7,\"reachDelta1d\":null,\"reachDelta7d\":null,\"reachDelta30d\":null},\"audience\":{\"targetedCountries\":[\"CA\",\"GB\",\"US\"],\"mainCountry\":\"GB\",\"gender\":null,\"ageMin\":null,\"ageMax\":null},\"rank\":{\"positionInPage\":11,\"currentRank\":11,\"rankDelta\":null,\"improvementPct\":6.08},\"flags\":{\"isEuAd\":null,\"isLowReach\":false,\"isMediaChanged\":true,\"hasPartnerBadge\":false}},{\"id\":\"facebook_946888944768303\",\"collationId\":\"1421680476176665\",\"platform\":\"facebook\",\"status\":\"active\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-12T04:57:40.376Z\",\"firstSeenAt\":\"2026-10-11T07:00:00.000Z\",\"lastSeenAt\":\"2026-11-07T05:42:55.017Z\",\"daysRunning\":47,\"media\":{\"type\":\"video\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://medias.trendtrack.io/facebook/thumbnails/8c88e4c3274e1caa51209cf575909f2c7778777ad7981de200017e66a384ec6a.jpg\",\"mediaUrl\":\"https://medias.trendtrack.io/facebook/video/98e966be5a27bc5397c999dd1b115bd9df4b0f00758781fd8b1d40951e5326cb.mp4\"},\"advertiser\":{\"id\":\"100217532825885\",\"name\":\"Blood Sugar Diary\",\"logoUrl\":\"https://medias.trendtrack.io/facebook/profile_picture/100217532825885.jpg\",\"facebookPageId\":\"100217532825885\",\"liveAdsCount\":250,\"reach30d\":345247,\"totalReach\":439746,\"countriesCount\":2,\"facebookLikes\":353,\"instagramFollowers\":null},\"content\":{\"title\":null,\"body\":\"🩸 Lower Your Blood Sugar Naturally — No Extra Meds, No Crashes\\n✅ Supports healthy fasting glucose & A1C levels \\n⚡ Kills the afternoon energy crash with clean, steady fuel \\n🔬 12x more potent than standard cinnamon capsules \\n💧 MCT Oil makes sure your body actually absorbs it — not just passes it \\n🌿 True Ceylon cinnamon — safe for daily long-term use \\n \\n👉 Try Primal Remedies today — and give your doctor something to smile about.\\nhttps://primal-remedies.com/pages/ceylon-cinnamon-7200mg-b-kid\",\"transcript\":\"If somebody whose blood sugar is making them pee three times a night took this blood sugar formula for 30 days, here's what would happen. Within the first 24 hours, the true silent cinnamon sourced from Sri Lanka lowers the blood sugar that's flushing the water out of your body, so you stop waking up three times a night to piss. After three days, you notice it stops your blood sugar from crashing, so your body stops chasing bread and sweets to bring it back up. And after seven days, cinnamalahide, the primary compound in silent cinnamon, slows the sugar hitting your blood after every meal. But what happens is what's worth it. You feel more energy. You start sleeping through the night. You have more peace of mind as your A1C levels start getting into normal range. After 14 days, lunch stops knocking you out cold on the couch. That's because the silent cinnamon stops the sugar surge that makes you tired as hell, so you can actually get done what you needed to do that same afternoon. After 17 and a half days, you notice that in the middle of day, you don't have that swollen feeling in your lower body like your feet, ankles, and legs. That's the blood sugar finally getting managed as it clears the sugar choking your body into inflammation. And after 30 days, all of that trapped sugar in your blood is moving into your cells the way it's supposed to. That A1C that was climbing up during every visit is finally heading down. Even your significant other notices your increased mood because you're sleeping normally again and you have more energy. But here's the thing. Real silent cinnamon only works if it's verified. Primal remedies that real verified silent cinnamon. It's sourced from Sri Lanka to ensure it contains cinnamaldehyde, which is the primary compound. And that's based on how it's harvested. It's third-party tested, completely cummeran-free, and suspended in MCT oil so it allows for maximum cellular absorption in the body. Unlike all of the fake silent cinnamon out there. Watch what really happens when you get your blood sugar under control so you can get your life back and stop having to worry. For a limited time, there is a special sale for silent cinnamon. And just remember to get the right kind, so go check out our Primal Remedy silent cinnamon in the link below.\",\"callToAction\":\"SHOP NOW\",\"landingPageUrl\":\"https://primal-remedies.com/pages/ceylon-cinnamon-7200mg-b-kid\",\"landingPageDomain\":\"primal-remedies.com\",\"ctaDescription\":\"90-Day Risk-Free Guarantee\",\"ctaLinkDescription\":null},\"metrics\":{\"reach\":107266,\"aggregatedReach\":null,\"estimatedSpend\":965,\"duplicates\":4,\"reachDelta1d\":2751,\"reachDelta7d\":5580,\"reachDelta30d\":77151},\"audience\":{\"targetedCountries\":[\"GB\",\"US\"],\"mainCountry\":\"GB\",\"gender\":null,\"ageMin\":null,\"ageMax\":null},\"rank\":{\"positionInPage\":5,\"currentRank\":5,\"rankDelta\":4,\"improvementPct\":2},\"flags\":{\"isEuAd\":null,\"isLowReach\":false,\"isMediaChanged\":true,\"hasPartnerBadge\":false}},{\"id\":\"facebook_4719977394988841\",\"collationId\":\"2992298264454021\",\"platform\":\"facebook\",\"status\":\"active\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-16T06:10:57.715Z\",\"firstSeenAt\":\"2026-10-15T07:00:00.000Z\",\"lastSeenAt\":\"2026-11-17T20:46:15.487Z\",\"daysRunning\":43,\"media\":{\"type\":\"video\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://medias.trendtrack.io/facebook/thumbnails/bd8898abb75fff90746ec3146ffda5eb84581a8af874dfb7b898863c017a6082.jpg\",\"mediaUrl\":\"https://medias.trendtrack.io/facebook/video/8d281a74ffe4ee4511edbe72b18c1f065d5bee2553163c3ca36cd7c03e4b9eed.mp4\"},\"advertiser\":{\"id\":\"100217532825885\",\"name\":\"Blood Sugar Diary\",\"logoUrl\":\"https://medias.trendtrack.io/facebook/profile_picture/100217532825885.jpg\",\"facebookPageId\":\"100217532825885\",\"liveAdsCount\":250,\"reach30d\":345247,\"totalReach\":439746,\"countriesCount\":2,\"facebookLikes\":353,\"instagramFollowers\":null},\"content\":{\"title\":null,\"body\":\"🩸 Lower Your Blood Sugar Naturally — No Extra Meds, No Crashes\\n✅ Supports healthy fasting glucose & A1C levels \\n⚡ Kills the afternoon energy crash with clean, steady fuel \\n🔬 12x more potent than standard cinnamon capsules \\n💧 MCT Oil makes sure your body actually absorbs it — not just passes it \\n🌿 True Ceylon cinnamon — safe for daily long-term use \\n \\n👉 Try Primal Remedies today — and give your doctor something to smile about.\\nhttps://primal-remedies.com/pages/ceylon-cinnamon-7200mg-b-kid\",\"transcript\":\"Let me answer this question for you all. Is it true you can flush all the sugar out of your blood through your urine? Yes. And it's something ninety eight percent of diabetics have no clue about. I'm a pancreatic cancer research doctor. I'm here to tell y'all the truth because if I were going to die tomorrow, I'd want every dietetic to stop asking God to deliver you from type two diabetes. He already sent the answer. Just let me explain. I always had a feeling the system was not designed for us, if you know what I mean. So today I'm going to put you all on to the three biggest lies they tell you about type two diabetes. By the end, you'll know how to address the real problem once and for all. Lie number one: Type two diabetes is caused by eating too much sugar or getting old. Not true. It's a cellular door disease. Let me explain. The doors on your cells stopped opening. When insulin knocks to move the sugar, nothing answers. So every gram of sugar from every meal stays trapped in your bloodstream with nowhere to go. That trapped sugar grinds through the lining of every blood vessel in your body, and that's been happening day after day, year after year, destroying your feet, your kidneys, your eyes and your heart. That's why cutting carbs, fasting or walking for hours does almost nothing. The doors are still closed and the sugar is still trapped. Lie number two, metformin or Ozempic fixes the problem. Y'all, that's ridiculous. Metformin tells your liver to make less sugar. It never opens the doors. Ozempic slows your stomach so less sugar enters your blood. It never opens the doors. None of them touch the trapped sugar that's already grinding through your vessels right now. It's like turning down the faucet while the drain is clogged, the water stays. Lie number three. Type two diabetes is irreversible. Y'all, that's what normal doctors want you to think. This one really grinds my gears and it's why I got into the field. SEARCH has identified two compounds from true saline cinnamon that address both halves of the problem at once. The first is called MHCP. It's a compound that signals the doors on your cells to start opening again, and once those doors open, the trapped sugar finally moves out of your blood and into your cells, where it gets burned for energy. The second is called cinnamalihide. It repairs the vessel lining the trapped sugar has been destroying for years. It helps your vessels produce nitric oxide again, the signal that tells them to relax and carry blood back to the places it stopped reaching: your feet, your kidneys, your eyes, your heart. Two compounds doing two jobs to fix the root cause. Let me be very clear here. I only recommend ceylon cinnamon from Primal Remedies, and I'll explain why shortly. But it's as easy as a couple of soft gels every day. Thousands of people are already using this to finally feel their feet again. They wake up with energy they haven't had in years. Here's the thing y'all, the current system would rather keep you on monthly prescriptions for the rest of your life than let you take these soft gels that cost less than a dollar a day. Primal Remedies is the only product that gets these two things right when it comes to verified saline cinnamon. One, it's DNA verified true saline cinnamon from Sri Lanka, not cassia from China like 90% of what's on shelves. Two, it's suspended in MCT oil so the fat soluble compounds actually cross your gut wall and reach your bloodstream instead of passing straight through you like every dry capsule on Amazon. No prescription your doctor has ever written offered you a refund. Every batch is third party tested before it reaches you, which is why it works, while the cheap cinnamon on Amazon does nothing for your blood sugar and quietly poisons your liver with coumarin while it does nothing. Tap the link below right now. And if the sale is live, consider yourself blessed. Don't waste this chance.\",\"callToAction\":\"SHOP NOW\",\"landingPageUrl\":\"https://primal-remedies.com/pages/ceylon-cinnamon-7200mg-b-kid\",\"landingPageDomain\":\"primal-remedies.com\",\"ctaDescription\":\"90-Day Risk-Free Guarantee\",\"ctaLinkDescription\":null},\"metrics\":{\"reach\":102183,\"aggregatedReach\":null,\"estimatedSpend\":920,\"duplicates\":3,\"reachDelta1d\":0,\"reachDelta7d\":0,\"reachDelta30d\":89853},\"audience\":{\"targetedCountries\":[\"GB\",\"US\"],\"mainCountry\":\"GB\",\"gender\":null,\"ageMin\":null,\"ageMax\":null},\"rank\":{\"positionInPage\":1,\"currentRank\":1,\"rankDelta\":1,\"improvementPct\":0.4},\"flags\":{\"isEuAd\":null,\"isLowReach\":false,\"isMediaChanged\":true,\"hasPartnerBadge\":false}},{\"id\":\"facebook_1472938208317970\",\"collationId\":\"1111291605240760\",\"platform\":\"facebook\",\"status\":\"active\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-11-19T18:21:18.543Z\",\"firstSeenAt\":\"2026-11-18T08:00:00.000Z\",\"lastSeenAt\":\"2026-11-26T18:07:12.781Z\",\"daysRunning\":9,\"media\":{\"type\":\"video\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://medias.trendtrack.io/facebook/thumbnails/e212e667541e9b3eb95a6b8127b50d99c438a0e9adb589b764f9b595f5f0d28a.jpg\",\"mediaUrl\":\"https://medias.trendtrack.io/facebook/video/135d81387f7623f2365a31791628da55e25ef929cb79a13fffb50b54c68feab6.mp4\"},\"advertiser\":{\"id\":\"169830089763759\",\"name\":\"Le Chercheur D'amour\",\"logoUrl\":\"https://medias.trendtrack.io/profile_picture/169830089763759.jpg\",\"facebookPageId\":\"169830089763759\",\"liveAdsCount\":1303,\"reach30d\":343865,\"totalReach\":427078,\"countriesCount\":2,\"facebookLikes\":314,\"instagramFollowers\":null},\"content\":{\"title\":null,\"body\":\"Looking to Support Healthy Blood Sugar Naturally? 🌿\\nExperience the Power of Primal Remedies Ceylon Cinnamon!\\n \\n✅ Helps support healthy blood sugar levels\\n✅ Supports steady daily energy & reduces crashes\\n✅ Enhanced with MCT oil for optimal absorption\\n✅ Authentic Ceylon cinnamon (concentrated 7,200 mg equivalent)\\n✅ Clean, research-backed ingredients for daily metabolic balance\\n \\nSupport healthier glucose levels naturally with a pure, high-potency formula built for daily stability.\",\"transcript\":null,\"callToAction\":\"SHOP NOW\",\"landingPageUrl\":\"https://primal-remedies.com/products/ceylon-cinnamon-7200mg\",\"landingPageDomain\":\"primal-remedies.com\",\"ctaDescription\":\"Buy 2 Get 1 Free\",\"ctaLinkDescription\":null},\"metrics\":{\"reach\":100058,\"aggregatedReach\":null,\"estimatedSpend\":901,\"duplicates\":3,\"reachDelta1d\":0,\"reachDelta7d\":0,\"reachDelta30d\":0},\"audience\":{\"targetedCountries\":[\"GB\",\"US\"],\"mainCountry\":\"GB\",\"gender\":\"all\",\"ageMin\":18,\"ageMax\":65},\"rank\":{\"positionInPage\":4,\"currentRank\":4,\"rankDelta\":0,\"improvementPct\":0.31},\"flags\":{\"isEuAd\":true,\"isLowReach\":false,\"isMediaChanged\":true,\"hasPartnerBadge\":false}}],\"pagination\":{\"page\":1,\"limit\":4,\"total\":12920,\"totalPages\":2500,\"offset\":0,\"isTotalApproximate\":true},\"meta\":{\"query\":\"primal-remedies.com\",\"keywords\":[],\"searchIn\":\"domain\",\"categoryIds\":[],\"country\":null,\"countryFilterKind\":\"audienceCountry\",\"adCountries\":null,\"mainCountries\":[],\"trendSignal\":\"reach_growth_7d\",\"sortBy\":\"reach\",\"order\":\"desc\",\"requestedLimit\":4,\"effectiveLimit\":4,\"activeOnly\":true,\"status\":\"all\",\"page\":1,\"minTrafficGrowthPercent\":null,\"trafficGrowthPeriod\":\"last30d\",\"trafficGrowth\":null,\"adsGrowth\":null,\"pageReachGrowth\":null,\"adReachGrowth\":null,\"language\":null,\"adLanguages\":[],\"cta\":[],\"currency\":null,\"currencies\":[],\"shopifyAppIds\":[],\"excludeShopifyAppIds\":[],\"pixelIds\":[],\"excludePixelIds\":[],\"themeIds\":[],\"filters\":{\"search\":[\"primal-remedies.com\"],\"searchType\":\"domain\",\"keywordMode\":\"any\",\"sortBy\":\"reach\",\"order\":\"desc\",\"page\":1,\"limit\":4,\"platforms\":[\"facebook\"],\"status\":\"all\"},\"warnings\":[\"Reported total remains exact, but totalPages is capped by pageable depth (offset<=10000).\"],\"paginationMaxOffset\":10000},\"fieldGuide\":{\"countryBreakdowns\":[{\"path\":\"data[].audience.targetedCountries\",\"meaning\":\"Full ad targeting country list, including non-EU markets such as US.\"},{\"path\":\"data[].audience.mainCountry\",\"meaning\":\"Primary audience country from Meta's EU/UK ad transparency data; null for ads outside that scope, even when the ad targets those markets.\"},{\"path\":\"data[].advertiser.countriesCount\",\"meaning\":\"Number of advertiser countries detected; not a country split.\"}],\"richNestedData\":[{\"path\":\"data[].collationId\",\"meaning\":\"Identifier of the combined creative represented by this search result. Pass it as scan_ad.collation_id to scan the same aggregate instead of only the representative ad.\"},{\"path\":\"data[].advertiser\",\"meaning\":\"Facebook page identity, reach, followers, and live ads.\"},{\"path\":\"data[].content\",\"meaning\":\"Ad copy, transcript fallback, CTA, and landing page.\"},{\"path\":\"data[].media\",\"meaning\":\"Media type, thumbnails, and media URLs.\"},{\"path\":\"data[].metrics\",\"meaning\":\"Reach, spend estimate, deltas, and duplicate metrics.\"},{\"path\":\"data[].audience\",\"meaning\":\"Country, gender, and age targeting fields.\"},{\"path\":\"data[].flags\",\"meaning\":\"EU, low-reach, media-changed, and partner-badge flags.\"}]},\"credits\":{\"requestedUnits\":4,\"effectiveUnits\":4,\"actualUnits\":4,\"costUnits\":6,\"recurringUnits\":6,\"topupUnits\":0,\"creditsRemaining\":9857,\"creditsSourceHeader\":\"recurring\",\"failurePhase\":null,\"releaseAttempted\":false,\"releaseSucceeded\":null}}","_meta":{"io.modelcontextprotocol/serverInfo":{"name":"trendtrack-server","version":"0.0.1"}},"structuredContent":{"requestId":"94c6110c-e90f-4f16-88ad-5382f93d7e6b","data":[{"id":"facebook_1088847760284220","collationId":"1395452092789787","platform":"facebook","status":"inactive","createdAt":"2026-09-13T05:51:59.406Z","firstSeenAt":"2026-09-12T07:00:00.000Z","lastSeenAt":"2026-10-05T08:31:30.991Z","daysRunning":23,"media":{"type":"image","thumbnailUrl":null,"mediaUrl":"https://medias.trendtrack.io/facebook/image/a33f135ac8bbad196a57ef191a8100ce376dabace75a4c3ac9f9bccac628493e.png"},"advertiser":{"id":"101838912282067","name":"Lisa Anderson","logoUrl":"https://medias.trendtrack.io/profile_picture/101838912282067.jpg","facebookPageId":"101838912282067","liveAdsCount":139,"reach30d":324,"totalReach":1188914,"countriesCount":3,"facebookLikes":299,"instagramFollowers":null},"content":{"title":null,"body":"My husband died a week ago.\n\nAnd there’s one photo on my phone I still can’t bring myself to delete.\n\nHe’s asleep in his recliner after dinner.\n\nMouth open.\n\nTV still on.\n\nGlasses and coffee sitting beside him.\n\nI took it because I thought it was funny.\n\nNow I look at that photo and wonder how many times his body was trying to tell us something we dismissed as “just getting older.”\n\nBecause that was our explanation for everything.\n\nThe naps after dinner.\n\nFalling asleep halfway through a movie.\n\nSaying he felt worn out even when he hadn’t done much that day.\n\nHe was 61.\n\nOf course he was more tired than he used to be.\n\nAt least that’s what we told ourselves.\n\nThen his cholesterol numbers started worrying his doctor.\n\nThat didn’t scare us much either.\n\nHe didn’t look sick.\n\nHe still cut the grass.\n\nStill drove our granddaughter to school when our daughter worked early.\n\nStill argued with our son about football every Sunday.\n\nStill complained whenever I bought the “healthy” bread.\n\nSo we did what we thought responsible people were supposed to do.\n\nWe changed breakfast.\n\nEggs became oatmeal.\n\nButter disappeared.\n\nI started checking labels at the grocery store.\n\nHe walked more.\n\nWe ordered fish instead of burgers.\n\nHe even stopped buying the cookies he’d eaten with his coffee for probably 20 years.\n\nEvery few months, there was another little sacrifice.\n\nAnd every time, he’d joke:\n\n“At this rate, you’ll have me eating cardboard by Christmas.”\n\nWe laughed.\n\nBut I could tell it bothered him.\n\nBecause food slowly stopped being something he enjoyed.\n\nIt became something he negotiated with.\n\nCan I eat this?\n\nHow bad is that?\n\nShould I skip dessert?\n\nMaybe I shouldn’t have the potatoes.\n\nAnd underneath all of it was the same belief:\n\nIf his cholesterol was high, he must still be eating the wrong foods.\n\nSo whenever his numbers weren’t where he wanted them, we blamed dinner.\n\nThen breakfast.\n\nThen snacks.\n\nThen ourselves.\n\nThat’s the part I keep thinking about now.\n\nBecause after he died, I sat at our kitchen table with his paperwork spread everywhere.\n\nOld blood work.\n\nAppointment notes.\n\nMedication lists.\n\nReceipts he’d stuffed into the same folder for reasons I’ll never understand.\n\nI wasn’t looking for anything specific.\n\nI think I just wanted to understand him.\n\nAnd somewhere between those pages, I realized how simplistic our thinking had become.\n\nWe had reduced cholesterol to a plate of food.\n\nEat the “bad” thing → cholesterol goes up.\n\nEat the “good” thing → cholesterol goes down.\n\nBut cholesterol is more complicated than any single breakfast or dinner.\n\nYour body produces cholesterol too, and factors beyond one meal can influence your overall numbers.\n\nThat sounds obvious when I write it now.\n\nIt didn’t feel obvious when we were standing in the grocery aisle debating whether he was “allowed” to buy cheese.\n\nThat realization sent me down a rabbit hole.\n\nNot because I thought I could go backward.\n\nI can’t.\n\nAnd I’m not going to pretend a supplement could have changed what happened to my husband.\n\nBut I needed to understand why we'd spent so much time treating every plate like it was the whole problem.\n\nEventually my reading led me to Ceylon cinnamon.\n\nI'd heard about cinnamon before.\n\nWhat caught my attention wasn't simply the ingredient.\n\nIt was how it was being delivered.\n\nCinnamon contains naturally occurring compounds including cinnamaldehyde.\n\nAnd cinnamaldehyde is fat-soluble.\n\nThat made me look differently at the dry cinnamon capsules I'd seen for years.\n\nPowder.\n\nCapsule.\n\nSwallow.\n\nDone.\n\nThen I found Primal Remedies.\n\nThey pair true Ceylon cinnamon from Sri Lanka with MCT oil inside an oil-based softgel.\n\nThe MCT oil acts as a lipid carrier for the fat-soluble cinnamon compounds.\n\nThey call the approach the Fat-Soluble Absorption Pathway.\n\nThat was what finally made the formulation make sense to me.\n\nNot “take more cinnamon.”\n\nThink about how the cinnamon is delivered.\n\nI also learned there is a meaningful difference between Ceylon cinnamon and the common cassia cinnamon most people recognize.\n\nCeylon naturally contains much lower levels of coumarin.\n\nAnd after everything I'd just been reading about health, I wasn't interested in blindly taking spoonfuls of random cinnamon from the kitchen cabinet.\n\nI wanted something simple that could fit beside the habits I was already trying to improve.\n\nSo I started using Primal Remedies Ceylon Cinnamon + MCT Oil as nutritional support alongside those habits.\n\nNot instead of eating well.\n\nNot instead of moving.\n\nAnd certainly not instead of speaking with a doctor and getting cholesterol checked.\n\nBecause if losing my husband taught me anything, it's that guessing how healthy someone is because they “look fine” isn't enough.\n\nLast Sunday, our daughter came over with the grandchildren.\n\nMy grandson climbed into Grandpa's recliner.\n\nSame chair from that photo.\n\nWithin 20 minutes, he was asleep sideways with one sock missing while everyone else was talking.\n\nFor half a second, I almost reached for my phone.\n\nThat's what I always did when his grandfather fell asleep like that.\n\nThen I stopped.\n\nThat chair doesn't make me laugh the same way anymore.\n\nBut it reminds me why I'm paying attention now.\n\nI don't want every meal to become a punishment.\n\nI don't want to spend the rest of my life afraid of breakfast.\n\nI just want to understand what I'm putting into my body, support it intelligently, keep getting my numbers checked, and be here for as many noisy Sunday afternoons with my family as I can.\n\nIf cholesterol has turned every plate in your house into a calculation, start by talking with your healthcare professional and understanding your actual numbers.\n\nAnd if you're already making healthier changes and want to learn about the Ceylon cinnamon + MCT oil approach I've added to my own routine, you can read about Primal Remedies below.\n\nBecause sometimes the photograph you thought was ordinary becomes the one that changes how you look at everything.","transcript":null,"callToAction":"LEARN MORE","landingPageUrl":"https://primal-remedies.com/pages/adv1-news-cinnamon","landingPageDomain":"primal-remedies.com","ctaDescription":"The Photo I Can't Look at the Same Way Anymore","ctaLinkDescription":"🚨 UPDATE: Ceylon Cinnamon 7200mg is SELLING OUT faster than expected! Lock in your order NOW to get 70% OFF + FREE Shipping"},"metrics":{"reach":132059,"aggregatedReach":null,"estimatedSpend":1189,"duplicates":7,"reachDelta1d":null,"reachDelta7d":null,"reachDelta30d":null},"audience":{"targetedCountries":["CA","GB","US"],"mainCountry":"GB","gender":null,"ageMin":null,"ageMax":null},"rank":{"positionInPage":11,"currentRank":11,"rankDelta":null,"improvementPct":6.08},"flags":{"isEuAd":null,"isLowReach":false,"isMediaChanged":true,"hasPartnerBadge":false}},{"id":"facebook_946888944768303","collationId":"1421680476176665","platform":"facebook","status":"active","createdAt":"2026-10-12T04:57:40.376Z","firstSeenAt":"2026-10-