{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018hbsSNmcj93bcjk7wkezCV","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"requestId\":\"62b1eae7-1bc0-4a1c-a373-d12a01f7d355\",\"data\":[{\"id\":\"facebook_4145937752382066\",\"platform\":\"facebook\",\"status\":\"active\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-11-26T18:35:34.892Z\",\"firstSeenAt\":\"2026-11-26T08:00:00.000Z\",\"lastSeenAt\":\"2026-11-26T18:35:52.140Z\",\"daysRunning\":1,\"media\":{\"type\":\"image\",\"thumbnailUrl\":null,\"mediaUrl\":\"https://medias.trendtrack.io/facebook/image/0cf006205b82dd7c6d4464a70efb127d6a53fd8b5c9e9187815d72e3261db6fa.jpg\"},\"advertiser\":{\"id\":\"1023030384228013\",\"name\":\"Tiana Brooks\",\"logoUrl\":\"https://medias.trendtrack.io/profile_picture/1023030384228013.jpg\",\"facebookPageId\":\"1023030384228013\",\"liveAdsCount\":188,\"reach30d\":76687,\"totalReach\":110959,\"countriesCount\":1,\"facebookLikes\":318,\"instagramFollowers\":null},\"content\":{\"title\":null,\"body\":\"I am here to tell Black people with Type 2 diabetes the TRUTH about their kidneys that their American doctors never will.\\n\\nAnd it's something 98% of them have no clue about.\\n\\nI spent 28 years as a dialysis nurse before I retired.\\n\\nIf I were going to die tomorrow, I would want every Type 2 diabetic to stop asking God to give them answers for their declining kidneys.\\n\\nBecause He already sent the answer.\\n\\nIs it true you can flush all the sugar out of your blood through your urine? Yes.\\n\\nBut the American system was not designed for Black people like us.\\n\\nSo I'm going to put you all on to the three biggest lies they tell you about Type 2 diabetes.\\n\\nBy the end, you'll know how to address the real problem once and for all.\\n\\nLIE NUMBER ONE.\\n\\nType 2 diabetes is caused by eating too much sugar or not being disciplined enough.\\n\\nChile, that is what they tell us. That is what they put in the pamphlets. That is what every Black woman I know has been told at least once sitting in a doctor's office.\\n\\nIt is not the truth.\\n\\nType 2 diabetes is a cellular door disease.\\n\\nLet me explain what that means.\\n\\nThe doors on your cells stopped opening. When insulin knocks to move the sugar out of your blood and into your cells where it belongs, nothing answers. The doors are stuck shut.\\n\\nSo every gram of sugar from every meal stays trapped in your bloodstream with nowhere to go.\\n\\nAnd that sugar does not sit there politely.\\n\\nIt grinds through the lining of every blood vessel in your body. The tiny vessels inside your kidneys. The ones your kidneys depend on to filter your blood. Day after day. Year after year. While you are taking your pill every morning and thinking something is being done about it.\\n\\nThat is what is destroying your kidneys. Not your discipline. Not your diet. Not your willpower.\\n\\nThe doors on your cells are closed, the sugar is trapped, and your kidney vessels are taking the full punishment for it.\\n\\nThat is why cutting out the mac and cheese does almost nothing. That is why putting down the cornbread does almost nothing. That is why walking for an hour every morning does almost nothing.\\n\\nThe doors are still closed. The sugar is still trapped. The damage is still happening.\\n\\nLIE NUMBER TWO.\\n\\nMetformin or Ozempic is fixing the problem.\\n\\nY'all. It is not.\\n\\nMetformin tells your liver to make less new sugar. It never opens the doors. The sugar that is already trapped in your blood is still there, still grinding against the vessel lining of your kidneys every hour you are alive.\\n\\nOzempic slows your stomach down so less sugar enters your blood after a meal. It never opens the doors either.\\n\\nIt is like turning down the faucet while the drain is still clogged. The water level in the sink keeps rising. The damage to your kidneys keeps happening underneath.\\n\\nI sat in dialysis rooms for 28 years watching the results of this exact lie.\\n\\nBlack men and women who had been on Metformin for a decade. Who had done everything the doctor said. Who showed up every three months, got their labs drawn, went home with refills, and believed they were being taken care of.\\n\\nAnd then one day their creatinine crept from 1.1 to 1.4 to 1.8.\\n\\nAnd then one day they were sitting in my chair. Three days a week. Four hours at a time. While a machine did the job their kidneys could no longer do.\\n\\nI know what a person looks like the first day they realize dialysis is going to be their life.\\n\\nI looked into those eyes for 28 years.\\n\\nI am not going to let that happen to you without telling you the truth they never told them.\\n\\nLIE NUMBER THREE.\\n\\nThe kidney damage from Type 2 diabetes is irreversible and you just have to manage it.\\n\\nThat right there grinds my gears the most.\\n\\nBecause I watched Black people believe it. And sit down. And stop fighting. And that broke my heart every single time.\\n\\nThe truth is that the two-front attack on your kidneys can be interrupted.\\n\\nThe trapped sugar can be pulled out through a completely different pathway. The vessel lining inside your kidneys can be supported and begin to recover. The inflammation grinding through your kidney tissue can be quieted.\\n\\nBut you will not hear that from the drug company that bills you hundreds of dollars a month for a prescription that never opens a single cellular door.\\n\\nYou will not hear it from the clinical guidelines that were written with pharmaceutical companies sitting at the same table.\\n\\nYou will not hear it from the doctor who has fourteen minutes to see you and a printer full of prescription pads.\\n\\nYou will hear it from me. Because I am retired. And I do not answer to a single one of them anymore.\\n\\nNow listen.\\n\\nThere is a compound system inside a spice that your grandmother probably had in her kitchen.\\n\\nTrue Ceylon cinnamon.\\n\\nI need you to hear me on this carefully, because there is a lot of confusion out there and people are spending money on the wrong thing.\\n\\nThe cinnamon in your spice rack is not it.\\n\\nThat is Cassia. A completely different species that comes from China. The active compounds your blood vessels and kidneys actually need are barely present in it. And it contains something called coumarin that is hard on your liver every time you take it.\\n\\nTrue Ceylon comes from Sri Lanka. The chemistry is completely different.\\n\\nAnd inside the bark of true Ceylon are two specific compounds that do what no prescription your doctor has ever written can do.\\n\\nThe first compound is cinnamaldehyde.\\n\\nIt activates something called GLUT4 translocation. Those are the cellular doors I told you about. The ones that stopped opening.\\n\\nCinnamaldehyde activates those doors through the same pathway that exercise uses. A completely separate pathway from insulin.\\n\\nThe trapped sugar finally moves. It leaves your blood. It goes into your cells where it gets burned for energy.\\n\\nThe sugar attack on your kidney vessels stops at the source.\\n\\nThe second compound is the proanthocyanidins concentrated in true Ceylon bark.\\n\\nThese are powerful antioxidant compounds that go directly to the vessel lining inside your kidneys. The lining that the trapped sugar has been grinding against for years.\\n\\nThey reduce the oxidative stress. They support the vessel walls.\\n\\nBlood reaches the kidney tissue again. The filtering system gets a chance to breathe.\\n\\nTwo compounds. Doing two jobs. Stopping the two-front attack on your kidneys that has been happening underneath your Metformin this whole time.\\n\\nYour doctor will never tell you about this. You cannot patent a tree. You cannot bill for it. So as far as they concerned, it does not exist.\\n\\nBut it exists in yours.\\n\\nNow here is the part that most people get wrong. And it is why most people who try cinnamon say it did absolutely nothing for them.\\n\\nThere are three failures built into almost every cinnamon supplement on the market. And every cheap bottle on the shelf gets at least two of them wrong.\\n\\nFailure one is the species.\\n\\nMost of them use Cassia instead of Ceylon. It is cheaper. It is everywhere. The active compounds your kidneys need are barely in it. You could take a Cassia capsule every day for a year and your blood vessels would notice almost nothing.\\n\\nFailure two is the dose.\\n\\nEven if a company uses real Ceylon, most capsules contain 500 to 1500 milligrams of dry powder. The clinical research that showed meaningful results used multi-gram daily doses. You cannot ask a 500 milligram capsule to do what 7,200 milligrams does. It is not even close.\\n\\nFailure three is the delivery. And this is the one nobody talks about.\\n\\nThe active compounds in Ceylon cinnamon are fat-soluble. They need fat to cross your gut wall and enter your bloodstream where they can actually reach your kidney vessels.\\n\\nA dry capsule carries no fat. Those compounds sit in your gut and pass straight through you.\\n\\nYou are paying for cinnamon that never reaches the place it needs to go.\\n\\nWrong species. Wrong dose. Wrong delivery. Three failures stacked on top of each other. And they still got the nerve to put it on the shelf next to the real thing.\\n\\nThat is the reason nothing you have already tried moved your numbers.\\n\\nThe brand that corrects all three is Metabolae.\\n\\nDNA-verified true Ceylon from Sri Lanka. Not Cassia from China. The real species, confirmed in a lab before it ever goes into production.\\n\\nConcentrated 12 to 1. One softgel delivers the equivalent of 7,200 milligrams of raw Ceylon bark. The dose that the research actually used.\\n\\nSuspended in organic MCT oil. The fat carrier that takes those fat-soluble compounds across your gut wall and into your bloodstream where they can reach your kidney vessels.\\n\\nNot a dry capsule. A softgel.\\n\\nThe difference between compounds that arrive and compounds that pass right through you.\\n\\nThird-party tested. Made in the USA in small batches.\\n\\nThat is the difference. Same spice. Right species, right dose, right delivery. Three failures corrected in one softgel.\\n\\nNow let me put y'all on to something before you go looking for this.\\n\\nDNA-verified true Ceylon cinnamon concentrated 12 to 1 and suspended in MCT oil is expensive to make right. It cannot be faked at drugstore prices.\\n\\nAnd because Metabolae has been spreading through communities like ours, knockoff brands have already started appearing with similar names and similar packaging. They look almost like Metabolae.\\n\\nInside the softgel is Cassia powder and filler oil. No DNA verification. No third-party testing. No idea what is actually in there.\\n\\nThat is why Metabolae only sells direct from their own site, not through Amazon, not through any chain retailer.\\n\\nBecause the moment a third party handles it, the counterfeit sitting next to it on the shelf undercuts the price and leaves you with something that does nothing while you think you are being helped.\\n\\nIf you are going to try this, only order from the official Metabolae site.\\n\\nI started taking one Metabolae softgel every morning with breakfast.\\n\\nWeek 2, y'all. I was sleeping through the night without getting up to use the bathroom three times. I had been doing that for over two years. The first morning I woke up and it was daylight I just laid there for a minute.\\n\\nWeek 4, my fasting glucose was 116. It had been sitting between 148 and 162 for three years.\\n\\nWeek 6, I had my labs drawn. My creatinine, which had been creeping up from 1.0 to 1.3 over four years, came back at 1.1.\\n\\nMy nephrologist looked at me across the desk. Asked me what I had changed.\\n\\nI told her about Metabolae. She pulled up the research on cinnamaldehyde and GLUT4 translocation right there in the room. Quiet for a second. Then she looked at me and said, Tiana, whatever you are doing, keep doing it.\\n\\nShe did not explain why she had never mentioned any of this in four years of watching my creatinine creep up.\\n\\nShe just said keep doing it.\\n\\nWeek 10, my A1C came back at 6.1. Down from 7.4.\\n\\nI have been telling every Black woman I know who is managing Type 2 about Metabolae. Every single one.\\n\\nMy cousin started on it six weeks after I did. She is 61, has had diabetes for nine years.\\n\\nHer creatinine was at 1.5. First labs after two months on Metabolae, down to 1.3.\\n\\nSleeping through the night for the first time in years. Says she has not felt this clear in the morning since before her diagnosis.\\n\\nA woman from my church started on it last month. Fasting glucose down from 171 to 134 in four weeks. Creatinine went from 1.6 to 1.4. She said her numbers moved more in one month than they had in four years on Metformin.\\n\\nWe talk about it every Sunday after service.\\n\\nBecause every day the doors are open is a day your body gets to start improving. The sugar is moving. The vessels are getting support. The kidneys are getting breathing room.\\n\\nAnd that is something nobody in the American medical system ever told us was possible.\\n\\nI know what that life costs a person. I know what it costs a family. I know what it steals from you and from everybody who loves you.\\n\\nAnd I know that most of the people I watched lose their kidneys were never told the truth until it was too late to use it.\\n\\nBut I am telling you now.\\n\\nIf your creatinine number has been creeping and your doctor said we should keep an eye on this.\\n\\nIf your A1C looks managed on paper while your kidney labs keep drifting in the wrong direction.\\n\\nIf you have been on Metformin for years and your numbers have never moved the way they promised.\\n\\nIf you have watched someone you love end up in a dialysis chair and you have been quietly terrified you are on the same road.\\n\\nYou are not crazy. You are not weak. You are not just getting older.\\n\\nBaby, you were just never told the truth.\\n\\nMetabolae has a Buy 2 Get 1 deal going right now. I ordered my three-month supply just last night. And last I checked they were running low on stock, so if you have been thinking about it, now is not the time to wait on your condition to get worse before you find out for yourself.\\n\\nDNA-verified true Ceylon from Sri Lanka. Concentrated 12 to 1. Suspended in organic MCT oil. Third-party tested. Made in the USA.\\n\\n90 days to try it. If your numbers do not move, if your sleep does not change, if the sugar does not shift, send back whatever is left in the bag and they refund every dollar. No paperwork. No questions.\\n\\nYou have 90 days and nothing to lose.\\n\\nYour kidneys have been waiting long enough.\\n\\n~ Tiana Brooks\\n\\nP.S. The morning my creatinine came back at 1.1, I sat in my car in the parking lot outside the lab and called my cousin. I read her the number. We were both quiet for a second. Then she said, Tiana, why did nobody ever tell us about this?\\n\\nI did not have an answer for that.\\n\\nI still do not.\\n\\nBut I am telling you now.\",\"transcript\":null,\"callToAction\":\"LEARN MORE\",\"landingPageUrl\":\"https://metabolae.com/pages/lp-ceylon-cinnamon-insulin-2\",\"landingPageDomain\":\"metabolae.com\",\"ctaDescription\":\"Ceylon Cinnamon 7200mg Equivalent with MCT Oil\",\"ctaLinkDescription\":\"Supports healthy blood sugar levels and metabolism with premium Ceylon cinnamon. Shop Metabolae's science-backed supplements. Free shipping available.\"},\"metrics\":{\"reach\":null,\"aggregatedReach\":null,\"estimatedSpend\":null,\"duplicates\":null,\"reachDelta1d\":null,\"reachDelta7d\":null,\"reachDelta30d\":null},\"audience\":{\"targetedCountries\":[\"US\"],\"mainCountry\":null,\"gender\":null,\"ageMin\":null,\"ageMax\":null},\"rank\":{\"positionInPage\":82,\"currentRank\":82,\"rankDelta\":0,\"improvementPct\":43.62},\"flags\":{\"isEuAd\":null,\"isLowReach\":false,\"isMediaChanged\":true,\"hasPartnerBadge\":false}}],\"pagination\":{\"page\":1,\"limit\":1,\"total\":1108,\"totalPages\":1108,\"offset\":0,\"isTotalApproximate\":false},\"meta\":{\"query\":null,\"keywords\":[\"ceylon\",\"Ozempic\"],\"searchIn\":\"ad_copy\",\"categoryIds\":[],\"country\":null,\"countryFilterKind\":\"audienceCountry\",\"adCountries\":null,\"mainCountries\":[],\"trendSignal\":\"reach_growth_7d\",\"sortBy\":\"newest\",\"order\":\"desc\",\"requestedLimit\":1,\"effectiveLimit\":1,\"activeOnly\":true,\"status\":\"active\",\"page\":1,\"minTrafficGrowthPercent\":null,\"trafficGrowthPeriod\":\"last30d\",\"trafficGrowth\":null,\"adsGrowth\":null,\"pageReachGrowth\":null,\"adReachGrowth\":null,\"language\":null,\"adLanguages\":[],\"cta\":[],\"currency\":null,\"currencies\":[],\"shopifyAppIds\":[],\"excludeShopifyAppIds\":[],\"pixelIds\":[],\"excludePixelIds\":[],\"themeIds\":[],\"filters\":{\"search\":[\"ceylon\",\"Ozempic\"],\"searchType\":\"adCopy\",\"keywordMode\":\"all\",\"sortBy\":\"newest\",\"order\":\"desc\",\"page\":1,\"limit\":1,\"platforms\":[\"facebook\"],\"status\":\"active\"},\"warnings\":[],\"paginationMaxOffset\":10000},\"fieldGuide\":{\"countryBreakdowns\":[{\"path\":\"data[].audience.targetedCountries\",\"meaning\":\"Full ad targeting country list, including non-EU markets such as US.\"},{\"path\":\"data[].audience.mainCountry\",\"meaning\":\"Primary audience country from Meta's EU/UK ad transparency data; null for ads outside that scope, even when the ad targets those markets.\"},{\"path\":\"data[].advertiser.countriesCount\",\"meaning\":\"Number of advertiser countries detected; not a country split.\"}],\"richNestedData\":[{\"path\":\"data[].collationId\",\"meaning\":\"Identifier of the combined creative represented by this search result. Pass it as scan_ad.collation_id to scan the same aggregate instead of only the representative ad.\"},{\"path\":\"data[].advertiser\",\"meaning\":\"Facebook page identity, reach, followers, and live ads.\"},{\"path\":\"data[].content\",\"meaning\":\"Ad copy, transcript fallback, CTA, and landing page.\"},{\"path\":\"data[].media\",\"meaning\":\"Media type, thumbnails, and media URLs.\"},{\"path\":\"data[].metrics\",\"meaning\":\"Reach, spend estimate, deltas, and duplicate metrics.\"},{\"path\":\"data[].audience\",\"meaning\":\"Country, gender, and age targeting fields.\"},{\"path\":\"data[].flags\",\"meaning\":\"EU, low-reach, media-changed, and partner-badge flags.\"}]},\"credits\":{\"requestedUnits\":1,\"effectiveUnits\":1,\"actualUnits\":1,\"costUnits\":2,\"recurringUnits\":2,\"topupUnits\":0,\"creditsRemaining\":9789,\"creditsSourceHeader\":\"recurring\",\"failurePhase\":null,\"releaseAttempted\":false,\"releaseSucceeded\":null}}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_019L7NbFA7MVTC5XoUdm43Uq","agent_id":"aabf4cd78d36d527d","session_id":"f17f1593-2f67-4602-83cb-0d79fa14ee5c","uuid":"b7d1f8de-64a4-4f0b-927f-1afa55841c9d","timestamp":"2026-11-27T18:50:16.129Z","tool_use_result":{"_meta":{"io.modelcontextprotocol/serverInfo":{"name":"trendtrack-server","version":"0.0.1"}}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_018hbsSNmcj93bcjk7wkezCV","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Conteos de saturación de ángulos"}
