{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RKkauUFtTm9goKvrdFVVzV","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"requestId\":\"8540424c-8ac2-49e3-bfed-4f9436f3cb1e\",\"data\":[{\"id\":\"facebook_1750297399367042\",\"collationId\":\"1575062660485075\",\"platform\":\"facebook\",\"status\":\"active\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-07T12:02:16.325Z\",\"firstSeenAt\":\"2026-10-07T07:00:00.000Z\",\"lastSeenAt\":\"2026-11-24T02:20:43.716Z\",\"daysRunning\":51,\"media\":{\"type\":\"video\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://medias.trendtrack.io/facebook/thumbnails/a620e6edf17bc48fa56572482ea6afe00af9349041151cfcf7b5898564fa900a.jpg\",\"mediaUrl\":\"https://medias.trendtrack.io/facebook/video/eae3fa6e3a7f09eaeca72382fb9cb76de429905e3d7c57fd97d5db7eb1664254.mp4\"},\"advertiser\":{\"id\":\"1106647162524028\",\"name\":\"Blood Sugar Balance Community\",\"logoUrl\":\"https://medias.trendtrack.io/profile_picture/1106647162524028.jpg\",\"facebookPageId\":\"1106647162524028\",\"liveAdsCount\":4312,\"reach30d\":1892898,\"totalReach\":3974228,\"countriesCount\":2,\"facebookLikes\":7770,\"instagramFollowers\":null},\"content\":{\"title\":null,\"body\":\"Looking to Support Healthy Blood Sugar Naturally? 🌿\\n\\nExperience the Power of Metabolae Sri Lankan Ceylon Cinnamon!\\n\\n✅ Helps support healthy blood sugar levels\\n✅ Supports steady daily energy\\n✅ Helps reduce blood sugar crashes\\n✅ Authentic Sri Lankan Ceylon cinnamon\\n✅ 200+ Clinical studies\\n✅ Enhanced with MCT oil for absorption\\n\\nSupport healthier glucose metabolism naturally with research-backed ingredients designed for daily stability.\",\"transcript\":\"Linda? Hey, Renee. What is that? Lunch. Your chart says nothing by mouths. I know. Then you know you're not supposed to be eating anything. Just watch. Watch what? My numbers. You were over four hundred three days ago. I know. And you're eating pizza? Check me after. I'm putting this in your chart. Go ahead. Well? $1.18. That's good, right? After pizza, fries, and pudding, that doesn't make sense. What are you doing? Checking your wristband. You think I'm somebody else? I think something doesn't add up. Linda Carter? That's me. She thinks I switched rooms with somebody. Let's check it again. 01/21. Three days ago, you were over 400. Your blood sugar came in at four twelve. Your a one c is 11.2. That's not possible. I take my metformin every day. Six years. I haven't missed a dose. This has been building for a long time. My doctor says I'm managed. Nothing by mouth until we get you stabilized, then we'll talk about starting insulin. Insulin? Let's get you through tonight first. 04:12. I'm sorry. I didn't mean to wake you. You didn't. Hospitals don't let anyone sleep. I heard him say met for men. Six years. I did everything he told me. I know you did. I prescribed metformin for thirty four years. You're a doctor? Endocrinologist. Retired. I told thousands of women exactly what your doctor told you. Cut the carbs, take the pill, you're managed. And it didn't work for them either? Not for most of them. I watched them lose feeling in their feet, lose their kidneys. I adjusted doses and called it care. I never once told them why the number wouldn't come down because nobody ever taught me. Then how do you know now? Because at 70, it happened to me. My a one c hit 8.1 on my own protocol. And a young Sri Lankan fellow I'd trained sat me down and embarrassed me in my own office. What did he tell you? That I had been treating the wrong thing for thirty four years. Every cell in your body has doors. Insulin knocks, the doors open, the sugar leaves your blood. After enough years, those doors stop answering. The insulin is there, the sugar is there, nothing opens. So the sugar stays in my blood, trapped, moving with every heartbeat, grinding through the vessels in your feet first. Do they burn at night? For two years? Then your kidneys, your eyes, your heart, and the metformin I prescribed for thirty four years, it tells the liver to make less new sugar. It never opens a single door. I was turning down the faucet for thousands of women while the drain stayed clogged. Then what opens them? That's what he showed me. True sealant cinnamon. Cinnamon. I laughed, too. Then he showed me the research. Published in the American Diabetes Association's own journal, a compound called MHCP signals those stuck doors to respond to insulin again. The trapped sugar finally moves into the cells. A second compound, cinnamaldehyne, repairs the vessel lining. The sugar has been grinding through. I've tried cinnamon pills. From Amazon? Yes. Kaseya, different tree, from China. Almost none of the compound in coumarin that burdens your liver. And even real Ceylon in a dry capsule is worthless. The compounds are fat soluble. No oil, it passes straight through you. This is what I've taken every morning for eight years. Metabolet. True Ceylon from Sri Lanka, DNA Verifieded, Concentrated twelve one, seventy thousand two hundred milligrams in one soft gel. Suspended in MCT oil so it actually reaches your blood. What's your a one c now? 5.5 at 78 off the metformin for six years. Why isn't your old office telling people this? Because it isn't a prescription. There's no rep, no insurance code. Take one when they let you eat, then have them check you. Your numbers are stable enough to send you home. We're holding off on the insulin. Good. But Linda, this doesn't end when you walk out that door. Follow-up with me in thirty days. I will. What are you taking? Ask the woman who used to sleep there. She prescribed metformin for thirty four years. The hip replacement? The endocrinologist. The doctor from the hospital gave you that? The doctor in the next bed. Cinnamon? Not the kind you're thinking of. You're not napping? Haven't napped in a week. Gary, my feet stopped burning. When? I don't know. I just noticed they're quiet. Seven point one. My a one c? Seven 0.1. You came into my ER at eleven point two. In a month? Fasting glucose averaging 100 o four. Whatever you're doing, keep doing it. 5.9. 5.9? I've been doing this twenty years. I don't see this. Neither did she for thirty four years. I took my metformin every day for six years. My doctor called me managed at every appointment. Then I woke up in an ER with a blood sugar of 412. The only person who ever told me the truth was a retired endonologist in the bed next to mine. She'd prescribed metformin for thirty four years. She told me it never opened a single door. Metabolai is true Ceylon cinnamon from Sri Lanka. DNA verified, concentrated 12 to one, suspended in MCT oil so it actually reaches your blood. One soft gel every morning. Buy two, get one free right now with a ninety day money back guarantee. If your numbers don't move, you pay nothing. Tap the link below. Don't wait until you're the one in the hospital bed.\",\"callToAction\":\"LEARN MORE\",\"landingPageUrl\":\"https://metabolae.com/products/softgels-ceylon\",\"landingPageDomain\":\"metabolae.com\",\"ctaDescription\":\"Ceylon Cinnamon 7200mg Equivalent with MCT Oil\",\"ctaLinkDescription\":null},\"metrics\":{\"reach\":253254,\"aggregatedReach\":null,\"estimatedSpend\":2279,\"duplicates\":13,\"reachDelta1d\":1846,\"reachDelta7d\":9336,\"reachDelta30d\":33503},\"audience\":{\"targetedCountries\":[\"GB\",\"US\"],\"mainCountry\":\"GB\",\"gender\":null,\"ageMin\":null,\"ageMax\":null},\"rank\":{\"positionInPage\":2,\"currentRank\":2,\"rankDelta\":0,\"improvementPct\":0.05},\"flags\":{\"isEuAd\":null,\"isLowReach\":false,\"isMediaChanged\":true,\"hasPartnerBadge\":false}},{\"id\":\"facebook_1280972764116331\",\"collationId\":\"2492196234615400\",\"platform\":\"facebook\",\"status\":\"inactive\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-06-21T13:41:59.006Z\",\"firstSeenAt\":\"2026-06-21T07:00:00.000Z\",\"lastSeenAt\":\"2026-10-15T15:50:13.649Z\",\"daysRunning\":116,\"media\":{\"type\":\"image\",\"thumbnailUrl\":null,\"mediaUrl\":\"https://medias.trendtrack.io/facebook/image/ed9f821fa80150dd1ea3adc6e39fa99dfd7c0a933bbd7572d1f891492d82e0f0.jpg\"},\"advertiser\":{\"id\":\"1018883361310799\",\"name\":\"Sandra Keller, RN\",\"logoUrl\":\"https://medias.trendtrack.io/profile_picture/1018883361310799.jpg\",\"facebookPageId\":\"1018883361310799\",\"liveAdsCount\":585,\"reach30d\":657004,\"totalReach\":4231542,\"countriesCount\":5,\"facebookLikes\":40683,\"instagramFollowers\":null},\"content\":{\"title\":null,\"body\":\"Here's what nobody tells diabetics about how to take Ceylon cinnamon correctly. And I say this as someone who spent a decade in metabolic research.\\n\\nBlood sugar is my thing. I'm Sandra Keller, and after 38 years as an ICU nurse, I've watched what uncontrolled glucose does to people over decades. I've seen the trajectory.\\n\\nCeylon cinnamon is the most studied natural compound for blood sugar control on the planet. It doesn't nudge your numbers down. It addresses why your cells stopped responding to insulin in the first place. The glucose buildup. The constant spikes. The crashes that follow.\\n\\nAnd here's the kicker.\\n\\nIt supports circulation and nerve function too. So if you're dealing with numbness, fatigue, or energy crashes on top of high blood sugar, you're hitting multiple problems at once.\\n\\nBut here's what the supplement industry doesn't want you to know.\\n\\nMost Ceylon cinnamon products are designed to look like they work. Not to work.\\n\\nThey sell you the wrong plant, in the wrong form, at the wrong dose. When your numbers don't move, they let you conclude that cinnamon doesn't work. It's one of the most profitable lies in the supplement space. And diabetics pay the price.\\n\\nHere's what they get wrong.\\n\\nA lot of people think any cinnamon supplement will do. That's true if you don't mind fake Cassia bark labeled as Ceylon.\\n\\nI learned this the hard way.\\n\\nMy fasting glucose had been running in the 180s for months. My A1C sat at 7.2 and wouldn't budge. I was doing everything right. Low carb. Exercise. Metformin twice daily. Still losing.\\n\\nI'd wake up at 3 AM to check my glucose out of habit. Still 165. Lie there until morning unable to fall back asleep. Brain fog by 2 PM every single day. Exhausted before my shift ended.\\n\\nMy doctor kept saying better control. Nothing was working.\\n\\nThen I found Ceylon cinnamon. Ordered softgels from Amazon. $14.99. Took them for two weeks.\\n\\nMy glucose dropped maybe 10 points. Better than nothing, but not life-changing.\\n\\nSo I went back to the research. I found two problems the supplement industry has never bothered to fix.\\n\\nThe first is species fraud.\\n\\n90% of cinnamon supplements are Cassia from China, labeled as Ceylon. This is not an accident. Cassia costs a fraction of what true Ceylon costs to source. The industry knows. They label it anyway. Cassia contains up to 250 times more coumarin, a compound that damages your liver with daily use. And it barely moves blood sugar at any dose.\\n\\nReal Ceylon from Sri Lanka has virtually zero coumarin and 12 times more of the active compounds that help. Without DNA verification on the label, you have no way of knowing which one you're swallowing.\\n\\nThe second problem is what most people never figure out.\\n\\nThe active compound in Ceylon cinnamon is cinnamaldehyde. It works at the cellular level to restore how your cells respond to insulin. It unlocks the door that glucose has been knocking on for years. But cinnamaldehyde is fat-soluble. Without a lipid carrier, it doesn't absorb. It passes right through your body unused.\\n\\nThe Journal of Food Science and Molecular Nutrition and Food Research both document this clearly. Fat-soluble compounds in a dry capsule cannot cross your cell walls. They reach your gut, find no fat carrier, and pass straight through.\\n\\nThe supplement industry knows this too. A softgel suspended in oil costs more to manufacture than a dry powder capsule. So they keep selling you the cheap version and letting you believe cinnamon doesn't work.\\n\\nIt works. They never gave it a way to reach you.\\n\\nWrong species, wrong form, wrong results. And they've been profiting from that gap for years.\\n\\nWhen you use real Sri Lankan Ceylon cinnamon concentrated and suspended in MCT oil, your body handles it differently. The oil carries cinnamaldehyde directly into your bloodstream, where it restores insulin sensitivity and helps your cells use glucose the way they're supposed to.\\n\\nAfter 38 years of watching patients suffer from bad advice, I'm particular about what I put in my body. So I only use Metabolae.\\n\\nTrue Ceylon from Sri Lanka. DNA-verified. Concentrated 12:1, so one softgel equals 7,200mg of whole cinnamon. Suspended in MCT oil for absorption. Third-party tested, coumarin-free, non-GMO, and gluten-free. Comes in a bag, not a bottle, which keeps the softgels fresher and the formula more stable.\\n\\nThe difference was immediate.\\n\\nDay three: I slept through the night. First time in 14 months.\\n\\nWeek one: The brain fog started lifting. I could focus during rounds without checking my notes three times.\\n\\nWeek two: My fasting glucose dropped from 187 to 142.\\n\\nWeek four: 118. I checked it three times because I didn't believe it.\\n\\nThree months later, my A1C dropped from 7.2 to 5.8. My doctor told me to keep doing whatever I was doing.\\n\\nI take it every single day now. Two years and counting. No liver damage. No gut problems. No side effects. Just steady energy, clear focus, and numbers that finally make sense.\\n\\nI've recommended Metabolae to six patients. All six came back with the same story. Better sleep within the first week. Brain fog lifting. Fasting glucose dropping. Numbers moving in the right direction.\\n\\nIf you're dealing with:\\n\\nFasting glucose that won't come down. Brain fog by mid-afternoon. Waking up multiple times at night. Energy crashes that hit like a wall. An A1C that barely budges despite your efforts.\\n\\nTry this. One softgel in the morning with breakfast. That's it.\\n\\nDon't waste money on cheap supplements. Most aren't even real Ceylon. They're Cassia from China, loaded with liver toxin, and they barely work. Even the real Ceylon ones come as dry powder that passes right through unused.\\n\\nWrong species, wrong form, wrong results.\\n\\nIf you're going to try Ceylon cinnamon, get the version that absorbs. True Ceylon from Sri Lanka, 7,200mg clinical dose, MCT oil suspension, third-party tested.\\n\\nThat's Metabolae. They offer a 90-day money-back guarantee because they believe everyone deserves access to liver-safe cinnamon that works. If your numbers don't improve, you pay nothing.\\n\\nThat's the only one worth taking.\\n\\nLet me know if you try it. I'd love to hear your experience.\\n\\n~ Sandra Keller, RN, ICU, 38 years\",\"transcript\":null,\"callToAction\":\"LEARN MORE\",\"landingPageUrl\":\"https://metabolae.com/pages/lp-ceylon-cinnamon-insulin-1\",\"landingPageDomain\":\"metabolae.com\",\"ctaDescription\":\"Ceylon Cinnamon 7200mg Equivalent with MCT Oil\",\"ctaLinkDescription\":\"Metabolae\"},\"metrics\":{\"reach\":242957,\"aggregatedReach\":null,\"estimatedSpend\":2187,\"duplicates\":8,\"reachDelta1d\":null,\"reachDelta7d\":null,\"reachDelta30d\":null},\"audience\":{\"targetedCountries\":[\"AU\",\"CA\",\"GB\",\"NZ\",\"US\"],\"mainCountry\":\"GB\",\"gender\":null,\"ageMin\":null,\"ageMax\":null},\"rank\":{\"positionInPage\":5,\"currentRank\":5,\"rankDelta\":null,\"improvementPct\":0.58},\"flags\":{\"isEuAd\":null,\"isLowReach\":false,\"isMediaChanged\":true,\"hasPartnerBadge\":false}},{\"id\":\"facebook_1017657837790383\",\"collationId\":\"886958824470092\",\"platform\":\"facebook\",\"status\":\"active\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-07-22T09:56:56.355Z\",\"firstSeenAt\":\"2026-07-22T07:00:00.000Z\",\"lastSeenAt\":\"2026-07-23T10:57:20.491Z\",\"daysRunning\":128,\"media\":{\"type\":\"image\",\"thumbnailUrl\":null,\"mediaUrl\":\"https://medias.trendtrack.io/facebook/image/30663f1a11df0dee1b92360a1135e201779f1a4b