{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AJUNWjUVTfrXZumbUJgzb1","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"requestId\":\"8672be16-fbbb-4127-9aa9-6f73c57710f9\",\"scope\":\"collation\",\"adId\":\"facebook_1163508329502617\",\"collationId\":\"1575062660485075\",\"representativeAdId\":\"facebook_1163508329502617\",\"memberAdIds\":[\"facebook_1163508329502617\",\"facebook_3404409543092867\",\"facebook_1847936819552375\",\"facebook_1162364506319664\",\"facebook_1396581432631718\",\"facebook_1381656900623073\",\"facebook_1072615535759885\",\"facebook_1158327930483340\",\"facebook_38980553821592974\",\"facebook_2137878790475443\",\"facebook_2911724399186328\",\"facebook_2147475512644561\",\"facebook_1750297399367042\"],\"activeAdIds\":[\"facebook_1163508329502617\",\"facebook_3404409543092867\",\"facebook_1847936819552375\",\"facebook_1162364506319664\",\"facebook_1396581432631718\",\"facebook_1381656900623073\"],\"memberAdsCount\":13,\"activeAdsCount\":6,\"memberAdIdsTruncated\":false,\"warnings\":[\"Reach history returned no numeric reach points, so trajectory is shown as unknown.\"],\"analysis\":{\"hook\":{\"text\":\"Linda? Hey, Renee.\",\"source\":\"ad_transcripts_hook\",\"sourceDescription\":\"Existing completed ad transcript hook.\",\"isFallback\":false},\"hookPattern\":\"unclassified\",\"hookPatternReason\":\"Hook text did not match a known opening pattern.\",\"trajectory\":\"unknown\",\"verdict\":\"History is inconclusive. Monitor the next few days before treating this as a scaler.\"},\"data\":{\"id\":\"facebook_1750297399367042\",\"collationId\":\"1575062660485075\",\"platform\":\"facebook\",\"status\":\"active\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-10-07T12:02:16.325Z\",\"firstSeenAt\":\"2026-10-07T07:00:00.000Z\",\"lastSeenAt\":\"2026-11-24T02:20:43.716Z\",\"daysRunning\":51,\"media\":{\"type\":\"video\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://medias.trendtrack.io/facebook/thumbnails/a620e6edf17bc48fa56572482ea6afe00af9349041151cfcf7b5898564fa900a.jpg\",\"mediaUrl\":\"https://medias.trendtrack.io/facebook/video/eae3fa6e3a7f09eaeca72382fb9cb76de429905e3d7c57fd97d5db7eb1664254.mp4\"},\"advertiser\":{\"id\":\"1106647162524028\",\"name\":\"Blood Sugar Balance Community\",\"logoUrl\":\"https://medias.trendtrack.io/profile_picture/1106647162524028.jpg\",\"facebookPageId\":\"1106647162524028\",\"liveAdsCount\":4312,\"reach30d\":1892898,\"totalReach\":3974228,\"countriesCount\":2,\"facebookLikes\":7770,\"instagramFollowers\":null},\"content\":{\"title\":null,\"body\":\"Looking to Support Healthy Blood Sugar Naturally? 🌿\\n\\nExperience the Power of Metabolae Sri Lankan Ceylon Cinnamon!\\n\\n✅ Helps support healthy blood sugar levels\\n✅ Supports steady daily energy\\n✅ Helps reduce blood sugar crashes\\n✅ Authentic Sri Lankan Ceylon cinnamon\\n✅ 200+ Clinical studies\\n✅ Enhanced with MCT oil for absorption\\n\\nSupport healthier glucose metabolism naturally with research-backed ingredients designed for daily stability.\",\"transcript\":\"Linda? Hey, Renee. What is that? Lunch. Your chart says nothing by mouths. I know. Then you know you're not supposed to be eating anything. Just watch. Watch what? My numbers. You were over four hundred three days ago. I know. And you're eating pizza? Check me after. I'm putting this in your chart. Go ahead. Well? $1.18. That's good, right? After pizza, fries, and pudding, that doesn't make sense. What are you doing? Checking your wristband. You think I'm somebody else? I think something doesn't add up. Linda Carter? That's me. She thinks I switched rooms with somebody. Let's check it again. 01/21. Three days ago, you were over 400. Your blood sugar came in at four twelve. Your a one c is 11.2. That's not possible. I take my metformin every day. Six years. I haven't missed a dose. This has been building for a long time. My doctor says I'm managed. Nothing by mouth until we get you stabilized, then we'll talk about starting insulin. Insulin? Let's get you through tonight first. 04:12. I'm sorry. I didn't mean to wake you. You didn't. Hospitals don't let anyone sleep. I heard him say met for men. Six years. I did everything he told me. I know you did. I prescribed metformin for thirty four years. You're a doctor? Endocrinologist. Retired. I told thousands of women exactly what your doctor told you. Cut the carbs, take the pill, you're managed. And it didn't work for them either? Not for most of them. I watched them lose feeling in their feet, lose their kidneys. I adjusted doses and called it care. I never once told them why the number wouldn't come down because nobody ever taught me. Then how do you know now? Because at 70, it happened to me. My a one c hit 8.1 on my own protocol. And a young Sri Lankan fellow I'd trained sat me down and embarrassed me in my own office. What did he tell you? That I had been treating the wrong thing for thirty four years. Every cell in your body has doors. Insulin knocks, the doors open, the sugar leaves your blood. After enough years, those doors stop answering. The insulin is there, the sugar is there, nothing opens. So the sugar stays in my blood, trapped, moving with every heartbeat, grinding through the vessels in your feet first. Do they burn at night? For two years? Then your kidneys, your eyes, your heart, and the metformin I prescribed for thirty four years, it tells the liver to make less new sugar. It never opens a single door. I was turning down the faucet for thousands of women while the drain stayed clogged. Then what opens them? That's what he showed me. True sealant cinnamon. Cinnamon. I laughed, too. Then he showed me the research. Published in the American Diabetes Association's own journal, a compound called MHCP signals those stuck doors to respond to insulin again. The trapped sugar finally moves into the cells. A second compound, cinnamaldehyne, repairs the vessel lining. The sugar has been grinding through. I've tried cinnamon pills. From Amazon? Yes. Kaseya, different tree, from China. Almost none of the