-11-24\",\"value\":22902},{\"date\":\"2026-11-25\",\"value\":22930},{\"date\":\"2026-11-26\",\"value\":22937}],\"instagramFollowersHistory\":null}},\"reachHistory\":[],\"credits\":{\"requestedUnits\":2,\"effectiveUnits\":2,\"actualUnits\":2,\"costUnits\":3,\"recurringUnits\":3,\"topupUnits\":0,\"creditsRemaining\":9466,\"creditsSourceHeader\":\"recurring\",\"failurePhase\":null,\"releaseAttempted\":false,\"releaseSucceeded\":null}}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_018c6j4BBLrReQGZf4cZL9L6","agent_id":"a5dca292aa3337a43","session_id":"f17f1593-2f67-4602-83cb-0d79fa14ee5c","uuid":"d5a72068-23b4-4633-a22f-8780e569c48f","timestamp":"2026-11-27T18:52:21.287Z","tool_use_result":{"_meta":{"io.modelcontextprotocol/serverInfo":{"name":"trendtrack-server","version":"0.0.1"}}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01X1STwZvHz6eP4QR6DG9teJ","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Extraer hooks del mercado Ceylon"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019BDuBxMfogwF8N6Ape6jjH","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"requestId\":\"daaca0ca-9646-4a58-a7a7-a2d1586b3357\",\"scope\":\"collation\",\"adId\":\"facebook_1126520220058709\",\"collationId\":\"1581740910311268\",\"representativeAdId\":\"facebook_1126520220058709\",\"memberAdIds\":[\"facebook_1126520220058709\",\"facebook_1008821168883591\",\"facebook_1818609795829252\",\"facebook_1069503926081878\",\"facebook_2133075447597782\",\"facebook_1381059210883028\",\"facebook_2063932491154970\",\"facebook_1116302141305643\",\"facebook_1529930345488454\",\"facebook_1410541540484741\",\"facebook_1409023367226295\",\"facebook_1934891194582712\",\"facebook_1481424820428105\",\"facebook_2856526661389818\",\"facebook_2174965626785539\",\"facebook_1098468079784783\",\"facebook_962680319433199\",\"facebook_2076210876330842\",\"facebook_1644394007113408\",\"facebook_1763419348115477\"],\"activeAdIds\":[\"facebook_1126520220058709\",\"facebook_1008821168883591\",\"facebook_1818609795829252\"],\"memberAdsCount\":20,\"activeAdsCount\":3,\"memberAdIdsTruncated\":false,\"warnings\":[\"Reach history returned no numeric reach points, so trajectory is shown as unknown.\"],\"analysis\":{\"hook\":{\"text\":\"Ray, wake up.\",\"source\":\"ad_transcripts_hook\",\"sourceDescription\":\"Existing completed ad transcript hook.\",\"isFallback\":false},\"hookPattern\":\"unclassified\",\"hookPatternReason\":\"Hook text did not match a known opening pattern.\",\"trajectory\":\"unknown\",\"verdict\":\"History is inconclusive. Monitor the next few days before treating this as a scaler.\"},\"data\":{\"id\":\"facebook_1763419348115477\",\"collationId\":\"1581740910311268\",\"platform\":\"facebook\",\"status\":\"active\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-09-12T03:26:27.376Z\",\"firstSeenAt\":\"2026-09-11T07:00:00.000Z\",\"lastSeenAt\":\"2026-09-29T01:26:44.563Z\",\"daysRunning\":77,\"media\":{\"type\":\"video\",\"thumbnailUrl\":\"https://medias.trendtrack.io/facebook/thumbnails/a17e2a97a8df448a2fc78f741def87b5710d8f60374fa8e44edd6a1ddd0f997f.jpg\",\"mediaUrl\":\"https://medias.trendtrack.io/facebook/video/76701e99ec22b7ff32e518cf034f9dbc09a93923a79a0d5dd73133d6029ea9f8.mp4\"},\"advertiser\":{\"id\":\"1106647162524028\",\"name\":\"Blood Sugar Balance Community\",\"logoUrl\":\"https://medias.trendtrack.io/profile_picture/1106647162524028.jpg\",\"facebookPageId\":\"1106647162524028\",\"liveAdsCount\":4312,\"reach30d\":1892898,\"totalReach\":3974228,\"countriesCount\":5,\"facebookLikes\":7770,\"instagramFollowers\":null},\"content\":{\"title\":null,\"body\":\"If your A1C is managed and there is still foam in your toilet every morning, your kidneys are telling you something your doctor is not. I'm Sandra Keller. Nephrology nurse. 22 years.\\n\\nI have been a nephrology nurse for 22 years. I have watched blood sugar dissolve kidneys from the inside out. I have sat beside patients and explained what dialysis means. I have watched people lose toes to neuropathy. I have watched someone go blind from complications.\\n\\nSo when a patient came to my clinic six months ago, type 2 for eleven years, A1C sitting at 6.8, on Metformin and a blood pressure pill, following every instruction, and his protein spillage had climbed to 510 while his feet had started tingling, I sat down and told him the truth. His numbers were managed. His kidneys were not.\\n\\nThree months later he came back. GFR 51. Protein spillage dropped to 280. Fasting glucose from 138 to 104. Neuropathy almost gone. I looked at his chart. \\\"What did you change?\\\" He reached into his jacket and set a bag on my desk. Ceylon cinnamon. Concentrated extract. 7,200mg in MCT oil. Metabolae.\\n\\nThat night I could not stop thinking about the GFR. GFR does not move like that. Not in three months. Not in a patient declining for two years. At 11:30 PM I started reading.\\n\\nYour A1C measures how much sugar is floating in your blood. That is all it measures. It does not see the tiny capillaries threading through your kidney tissue. It does not see the nerves in your feet. A 6.8 can be managed and your kidney filters can still be quietly wearing down behind it.\\n\\nThe tiny filters inside your kidneys have been under sustained pressure from glucose for years. They start to fail. Protein leaks out. Your feet start to burn. The damage that leads to dialysis is already happening while your doctor says managed. That neuropathy is not a warning sign. It is evidence that kidney failure is already happening.\\n\\nEvery cell has doors. GLUT4 transporters. Insulin gives the signal, they open, sugar moves into the cell. In insulin resistance, those doors stop responding. The sugar stays in your blood. Keeps grinding through every small vessel. Kidney capillaries. Nerves in your feet. Year after year.\\n\\nMetformin tells your liver to produce less sugar. It reduces the flood. But it does not touch the doors. The sugar that remains keeps grinding. The drug that reduced the flood did not open the drain.\\n\\nThere is a compound that triggers the doors directly. MHCP. Found in true Ceylon cinnamon. Not cassia. When the doors open, glucose clears from the blood. The pressure on the kidney filters drops. The neuropathy pain lessens. The protein spillage drops. The drain opens. Your medications manage the flood. This opens the drain. Both together is the full answer.\\n\\nBut most cinnamon products are cassia. Wrong plant. Cassia burdens your liver at therapeutic doses. And even real Ceylon in a dry capsule does not absorb. The active compounds are fat-soluble. Without oil, they pass straight through. Your cinnamon did not fail because cinnamon does not work. It failed because it was never delivered.\\n\\nMetabolae. True Ceylon. DNA-verified from Sri Lanka. 7,200mg. 12 to 1 concentrated extract. Suspended in MCT oil. Third-party tested. The same bag that patient set on my desk.\\n\\nI went home and ordered a bag. Week 2, my fasting glucose dropped from 112 to 98. Week 3, the 3 AM trips stopped. Sleeping through the night for the first time in a year. Week 10, my creatinine came back at 1.0. It was 1.3 six months earlier. My colleague looked at it. \\\"What did you change?\\\" \\\"Keep doing whatever you're doing.\\\"\\n\\nThat patient came back. GFR 54. Up from 46. Protein spillage 195. Down from 510. Tingling gone. He smiled. \\\"The drain opened.\\\" I have recommended Metabolae to nine patients. Every single one. Same pattern. One woman, 61, spillage down 40 percent. She cried when the foam was gone. Another patient's GFR went from 51 to 57. His nephrologist said the trajectory had changed.\\n\\nIf you are sitting with a managed A1C while your kidney markers decline. While the foam is still there. While your feet still tingle. While the fear of dialysis grows bigger every year. Try Metabolae risk-free. 90-day guarantee. If your numbers do not move, you pay nothing. One softgel daily with breakfast. The flood is being managed. The drain was never opened. You know now that it can be. Tap below.\",\"transcript\":\"Ray, wake up. I need you to drive me to the hospital now. What, Sandra? Is it indigestion again? No. It's central pressure radiating to my jaw. I'm losing my breath. This is the exact situation I've been describing to patients for the last twenty years. We're going. Get dressed right now. I never thought I'd be the one placing a stent in a cardiologist, especially not the one who personally trained me. Let's get this done. I don't want to end up like my father. He was type two two. Died from a heart attack at 64. Yes, ma'am. Don't worry. Everything's going to be fine. Sandra, I don't have good news. Go ahead. Your eGFR dropped from 89 to 71. I'm afraid it's early stage two diabetic nephropathy. How? I mean, nobody flagged it. Your A1C has always been managed. The algorithm didn't trigger a referral. So that's five organs now. Specialist found small hemorrhages in both eyes. Early background retinopathy. The hepatologist ordered a liver ultrasound. Grade two hepatic steatosis. Podiatry found measurable peripheral neuropathy in both feet, right worse than left. And now, early stage two diabetic nephropathy. I'm sorry. Priyanka, your a one c was 7.8. Now it's 5.6. You came off lisinopril twenty months ago. What are you doing? Doctor, I didn't think you'd take it seriously. Try me. My aunt Kumardy, she's from New Jersey. She's been telling us about this thing for years. Telling you what? Just go see her, please. This is an address? She knows things modern medicine hasn't told us. I'll go this Saturday. Your medications are fighting the wrong battle. You know this. That's why you're sitting at my kitchen table. I read the mechanism studies just before coming here. Now I understand it clinically. This one is your feet. This one is your kidneys. This one is your eyes. This one is your liver. And this one is your heart. Your specialist told you that you have five different problems. When in reality, it's one problem. The same trapped sugar grinding through all five organs. The metformin quieted my glucose number. Lisinopril lowered my pressure. The statin reduced my LDL. But exactly. Three numbers on three chart lines. Below all three, the trapped sugar's been grinding through your vessels every heartbeat year after year. Now here's what nobody taught you in medical school. For over one thousand years, the women in my grandmother's village have been using one thing for this: true Ceylon cinnamon, not Cassia. Cassia is a different plant, cheaper from China, and it has two fifty times more coumarin, which strains your liver. What does real Ceylon do? It has two compounds. One is called MHCP. It opens the cellular doors. Your training says are managed by insulin. Once the doors open, the trapped sugar finally moves out of your bloodstream and grinding stops. The second compound is cinnamaldehyde. It repairs blood vessels that the trapped sugar damaged. The vesse